<header><p class="st-kicker">other · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Lordship of Ameland</h1><p class="st-meta">1424 CE – 1704 CE (approx.) · capital Hollum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Wadden Sea island that remained a free lordship under the Cammingha family, neutral in the wars around it, until the Orange-Nassau family bought it.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ameland lay outside the authority of the counts of Holland and the Frisian lands, and from the 15th century the Cammingha family, Frisian chieftains, ruled it as lords, a status the register dates to 1424. They defended its independence against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> provinces.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The island was small, with villages such as Hollum, Ballum and Nes, living from fishing, farming and later whaling, with many 17th-century whaling commanders. Its lords claimed neutrality, which let islanders trade during wars. Ameland accepted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> and governed itself through local courts under the lord.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the Cammingha line ended, the lordship was bought in 1704 for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-orange-nassau">Orange-Nassau</a> family. It lost its separate status in the Batavian period and became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-frisia">Friesland</a> in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Kingdom of the Netherlands</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/lordship-of-ameland.jpg" alt="Lordship of Ameland" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Original by Nikio. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Ameland.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1424 CE – 1704 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Hollum</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Reformed Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>West Frisian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Netherlands</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ameland</dd></dl></aside></div>
